      "text": "// Whether we have started executing any user-provided CJS code.\n// This is set right before we call the wrapped CJS code (not after,\n// in case we are half-way in the execution when internals check this).\n// Used for internal assertions.\nlet _hasStartedUserCJSExecution = false;\n// Similar to _hasStartedUserCJSExecution but for ESM. This is set\n// right before ESM evaluation in the default ESM loader. We do not\n// update this during vm SourceTextModule execution because at that point\n// some user code must already have been run to execute code via vm\n// there is little value checking whether any user JS code is run anyway.\nlet _hasStartedUserESMExecution = false;\n"
    },
    {
      "source": "C:\\Users\\adyba\\pi-zig\\main\\verification\\node-module-constructor-sourceonly-20261016\\authority\\lib__internal__modules__helpers.js.txt",
      "lines": [
        478,
        489
      ],
      "bytes": 318,
      "sha256": "E21C7905DB7E403B899DF3D0D3236BE2E0A2E954328F815AF2163C893F1B4940",
      "text": "  hasStartedUserCJSExecution() {\n    return _hasStartedUserCJSExecution;\n  },\n  setHasStartedUserCJSExecution() {\n    _hasStartedUserCJSExecution = true;\n  },\n  hasStartedUserESMExecution() {\n    return _hasStartedUserESMExecution;\n  },\n  setHasStartedUserESMExecution() {\n    _hasStartedUserESMExecution = true;\n  },\n"
    },
    {
      "source": "C:\\Users\\adyba\\pi-zig\\main\\verification\\node-module-constructor-sourceonly-20261016\\authority\\lib__internal__modules__cjs__loader.js.txt",
      "lines": [
        1796,
        1817
      ],
      "bytes": 814,
      "sha256": "B8D91080C077B857BCB4DB94148A71C85F72E8E0DBA51AA326B95A6A5551A7B7",
      "text": "  }\n\n  const dirname = path.dirname(filename);\n  const require = makeRequireFunction(this, redirects);\n  let result;\n  const exports = this.exports;\n  const thisValue = exports;\n  const module = this;\n  if (requireDepth === 0) { statCache = new SafeMap(); }\n  setHasStartedUserCJSExecution();\n  this[kIsExecuting] = true;\n  if (this[kIsMainSymbol] && getOptionValue('--inspect-brk')) {\n    const { callAndPauseOnStart } = internalBinding('inspector');\n    result = callAndPauseOnStart(compiledWrapper, thisValue, exports,\n                                 require, module, filename, dirname);\n  } else {\n    result = FunctionPrototypeCall(compiledWrapper, thisValue, exports, require, module, filename, dirname);\n  }\n  this[kIsExecuting] = false;\n  if (requireDepth === 0) { statCache = null; }\n  return result;\n};\n"
    }
  ],
  "semantic_accounting": [
    "Two private native booleans have the original false initial values; each Source setter sets exactly one to true and returns undefined, and each getter returns the corresponding boolean.",
    "All four methods are real ordinary nonconstructible zero-argument callables with original names. Receiver/arguments are ignored without property access or coercion.",
    "The actual per-Engine private cache retains one helper carrier and shared cell. Acquiring it again returns the same methods without resetting facts. Native cell and callable captures are charged and traced/finalized through existing owners.",
    "Canonical prototype Inputs no longer accepts set_started_user_cjs. Its real bootstrap captures setHasStartedUserCJSExecution from this helper owner; the original compile-body call remains byte-for-byte at the same point before wrapper execution.",
    "The ESM sibling getter/setter are complete original lexical operations only. No ESM evaluation, inspector, permission policy, diagnostics channel or loader publication is synthesized."
  ],
  "prototype_inverse": {
    "removed_input_line": "    set_started_user_cjs: c.JSValue,\n",
    "added_capture": "    // Original internal/modules/helpers owns this lexical fact. It is shared\n    // with its getters/ESM sibling and is not supplied by the embedding caller.\n    const execution_state = try s.own(try @import(\"native_node_module_execution_state.zig\").acquire(engine));\n    try s.put(roots, \"set_started_user_cjs\", try s.get(execution_state, \"setHasStartedUserCJSExecution\"));\n",
    "anchor": "    inline for (.{ .{ \"kFormat\", constructor.LoaderKey.format }",
